WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
A thirty kilogram child sits on a seesaw,

2
00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.510
two point four metres from the pivot.

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.370
Then an adult with twice
the mass, sixty kilograms,

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.290
climbs on the other side.

5
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.830
So where must the adult sit
for the plank to balance?

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.200
Twice as far out?

7
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.670
The same distance, leaning back?

8
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.180
In this mission, you'll measure
the turning effect of a force:

9
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.860
its moment, the force times its
perpendicular distance from the pivot.

10
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.720
For balance, the clockwise moments
must equal the anticlockwise moments.

11
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.590
And you'll model the
plank as a uniform rod,

12
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.080
whose weight acts at its midpoint.

13
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:40.120
Your mission: find where
the adult must sit.
